anyOS Hardware Firmware Directory
=================================

This directory contains firmware blobs required by hardware drivers.
These are proprietary binaries provided by hardware vendors under
redistributable licenses.

Source: Linux Firmware Repository
  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git
  https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git/tree/

On a Linux system, firmware files are typically found at /lib/firmware/.


wifi/
-----
  Intel WiFi (iwlwifi):
    iwlwifi-cc-a0-77.ucode          - AX200
    iwlwifi-ty-a0-gf-a0-77.ucode    - AX210/AX211
    iwlwifi-so-a0-gf-a0-77.ucode    - AX201
    iwlwifi-9260-th-b0-jf-b0-46.ucode - AC 9260

  Qualcomm Atheros (ath10k/ath11k):
    ath10k_QCA6174_hw3.0_firmware-6.bin
    ath10k_QCA6174_hw3.0_board.bin

  Realtek USB WiFi:
    rtl8188eu.bin                    - RTL8188EU/EUS

gpu/
----
  (reserved for future GPU firmware, e.g. AMD Radeon microcode)

bluetooth/
----------
  Intel Bluetooth:
    ibt-20-1-3.sfi                   - AX200/AX201 BT firmware
  (reserved for future Bluetooth firmware)


To populate: Copy the required files from /lib/firmware/ on any
Linux installation, or download from the git repository above.
